# Lathe kiosk — environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev, or set these in the Vercel project
# (Settings → Environment Variables). ALL of these are optional: with none set,
# the app runs as the fully local, demo-seeded kiosk used for the Vercel preview.
# Only `VITE_`-prefixed vars are exposed to the browser bundle — never put a
# database service key or any server-only secret here.

# --- Live analytics ingestion (leave BOTH blank to stay local-only/demo) ---
# Base URL of the ingestion API, e.g. https://api.meetlathe.com. When set
# together with VITE_KIOSK_KEY, the kiosk routes events to `${VITE_API_URL}/events`
# instead of buffering to localStorage only.
VITE_API_URL=
# Scoped, ingest-only kiosk key (NOT a database key). Sent as the X-Kiosk-Key
# header. Least privilege: it can write leads/events for its show and nothing else.
VITE_KIOSK_KEY=

# --- Privacy notice shown on the lead form's consent line ---
# Defaults to https://meetlathe.com/privacy if unset. Point at the exhibitor's
# per-show privacy URL for a live event.
# VITE_PRIVACY_URL=
